        "answer": {
          "short": "a(iii), b(iii), c(ii) and f(ii).",
          "worked": "a(iii): $\\frac12x-1=(\\frac12x+1)-2$, so shift down $2$.\n\nb(iii): $-x-4=(4-x)-8$, so shift down $8$.\n\nc(ii): $(x+1)^2=((x+2)-1)^2$, so shift left $2$.\n\nf(ii): if $f(x)=1+\\frac1{x-1}$, then $f(x+2)-2=-1+\\frac1{x+1}$, so shift left $2$ and down $2$.\n\nThe remaining targets change the line's gradient, the parabola's opening direction, the square-root graph's orientation, the exponential's direction or sign, or the reciprocal branches' orientation; translations cannot make those changes.",
